msgid "Login Hardening"
msgstr ""

#. Plugin URI of the plugin
#: wp-login-hardening.php
msgid "https://github.com/bluantinoo/wp-login-hardening"
msgstr ""

#. Description of the plugin
#: wp-login-hardening.php
msgid "Takes away what a brute force needs: the list of real usernames, a login form that tells a wrong name from a wrong password, XML-RPC, accounts nobody should use. Optionally logs every failed attempt for fail2ban."
msgstr ""

#. Author of the plugin
#: wp-login-hardening.php
msgid "Diego Vagnoli"
msgstr ""

#. Author URI of the plugin
#: wp-login-hardening.php
msgid "https://diegovagnoli.it"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: reason.
#: includes/fail2ban.php:187
#, php-format
msgid "Test line not written: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/fail2ban.php:195
msgid "Test line not written: the client address cannot be determined. The request comes from a trusted proxy, and the last entry of X-Forwarded-For is missing, invalid or itself a trusted proxy. As things stand, nothing would be logged."
msgstr ""

#: includes/fail2ban.php:205
msgid "Test line handed to syslog. Look for it in the log that receives the auth facility, usually /var/log/auth.log. If it is not there, PHP cannot reach syslog (for example a chrooted PHP-FPM pool): use a log file instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/fail2ban.php:206
msgid "Syslog refused the test line."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: file path.
#: includes/fail2ban.php:214
#, php-format
msgid "Test line written to %s."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: file path.
#: includes/fail2ban.php:216
#, php-format
msgid "Could not write to %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/fail2ban.php:294
msgid "The log file path must be absolute."
msgstr ""

#: includes/fail2ban.php:296
msgid "The log file name must end in .log."
msgstr ""

#: includes/fail2ban.php:298
msgid "The folder of the log file does not exist."
msgstr ""

#: includes/fail2ban.php:300
msgid "The log file must be outside the folders the web server serves."
msgstr ""

#: includes/fail2ban.php:302
msgid "PHP cannot write the log file."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:126
msgid "Hide usernames"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:127
msgid "Visitors who are not logged in get no user list from the REST API, no redirect from ?author=N to the author page, no author archives, and oEmbed shows the site instead of the author."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:130
msgid "Same error for a wrong name and a wrong password"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:131
msgid "An unknown username or email gets the message WordPress gives for a wrong password, so the login form no longer confirms which names exist."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:134
msgid "Turn off XML-RPC"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:135
msgid "No XML-RPC methods, pingbacks included, not even those added by other plugins, and the X-Pingback header and RSD link are removed. Leave it off if the site uses Jetpack, the WordPress mobile app or remote publishing. With it on, WooPayments and the WooCommerce mobile app lose the Jetpack connection, and a translation service connected to WPML can no longer deliver: set WPML's Translation pickup mode to \"The site will fetch translations manually\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:138
msgid "Accounts without a role cannot log in"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:139
msgid "Retired accounts and author-only accounts can keep their content: remove their role and they can never log in again, and sessions they already have stop working. Not available on multisite."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:142
msgid "Turn off application passwords"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:143
msgid "Application passwords let an app call the REST API with a password alone, which bypasses two-factor login. Leave them on if an integration uses them; WooCommerce REST API keys are a separate mechanism and keep working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:146
msgid "Log attempts for fail2ban"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:147
msgid "Writes a line for every failed login, password reset request and blocked attempt, in the format of the WP fail2ban plugin. Useful only if you run fail2ban on the server."
msgstr ""

